The ReplicaSyncSession class and its related types are internal, and the SyncStatusInfo struct is internal as well. This means I cannot directly instantiate or subclass ReplicaSyncSession in a test project outside the assembly.

Since the logging call is inside an internal method, and the class is internal, the best approach is to create a test class inside the same assembly (or use InternalsVisibleTo attribute if available) to test the logging behavior. However, I don't have evidence of InternalsVisibleTo being set.

Given the constraints, I will write a test class inside the same namespace and mark it as internal, assuming the test project is part of the same assembly or can access internals. I will mock ILogger and simulate the exception to verify the LogError call.

I will submit a test file with internal access and the necessary mocks to cover the LogError call on line 203 (WaitForSyncCompletionAsync).

